.Dd February 1, 2026
.Dt DRIVER_DETACH 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm driver_detach
.Nd unbind a driver from a device
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In kern/driver.h
.Ft int
.Fn driver_detach "struct device *dev"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn driver_detach
function unbinds the currently attached driver from the device
.Fa dev .
.Pp
The function performs the following steps:
.Bl -enum
.It
Verifies that the device is currently bound to a driver.
.It
Calls the
.Va detach
callback of the driver (if provided).
.It
Clears the
.Va dev->driver
pointer, setting it to NULL.
.El
.Pp
If the device is attached to a bus, the bus lock is held during the unbinding process.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn driver_detach
function returns 0 on success.
Otherwise, it returns -1 to indicate failure (e.g., invalid arguments, device not bound, or detach callback returned failure).
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr driver_attach 9 ,
.Xr driver_register 9 ,
.Xr device_unregister 9
